On my third Saturday, I stood ready behind the counter.
I have finally learned to relax a bit in the café.
Through the window, I saw an older man on the street.
He walked slowly towards the front door.
He was also here on my first and my second shift.
He is one of the café's regular customers.
I have learned to remember his order by heart.
He always buys exactly the same thing.
He opened the door and came up to the register.
I looked at him and smiled.
"Good morning," I said.
"Should I make your usual cortado?"
The man looked at me surprised.
Then he smiled happily.
"Yes please, I would very much like that," he answered.
I went over to the espresso machine.
I have made coffee many times now, so it went quickly.
It was a good feeling to know our guests.
